Just a VERY minor quibble.

I have patch level 7 of PC nethack, I ftped the distribution disks from
somewher, I don't remember exactly where.

Anyway the graphics option is set to take advantage of some of the PC's
graphics character set, so fountains look a little more like fountains,
hallways are a shaded rectangle instead of #, etc.

Now if in the game you use ? to get help when it lists what different symbols
mean it uses the default unix character set rather than the default PC set.
(At least I'm assuming it's the unix default, it's what they have here on
andrew.)  Since I already knew what I was doing, this isn't much of a problem,
but it seems that the help given in the game should be accurate to help new
players.

The best solution would be to have help look at the options setting and show
the current defined character set, but this would probably take a little bit
of work since I believe all it does now is show the contents of a file in
your \games\nethack directory.

But at least the game could be packaged with that file modified to reflect the
default character set in the distribution package.

Another thing I have noticed is that several of my friends (but not me) prefer
the unix character set to the default pc set.  They spent quite a bit of time
modifing their graphics option to make is match the unix set.  As it is
the distribution nethack.cnf contains several alternate character sets
which are commented out at first.  How about adding the unix set to the
alternate sets provided??

Thanks to the developers for a great game.

